 "rule": "(applied case by case; the class string of a case decides only where the rule gives the same answer for\nevery case of that string):\n  CELL: the fault shows in a value the sentence says, against the cell or row its marker cites, or in arithmetic\n    between cited cells: a wrong number, number word ('half', 'twice', 'tripled', 'a third', a typed sign), name,\n    title, date or time; a calculation; a marker grammar fault (no marker, a bad path, two results, a forged\n    marker); a value bound to the wrong ROW (another row's cell, a period row called by another row's label, a\n    totals cell said of a row, a row's cell said of the totals, a row placed in a group its row does not name) or to\n    the wrong MEASURE (openings as videos, days as videos, a count as a share or a difference, points as a percent,\n    the Shorts share as the long share, now and before swapped into 'from ... to', a share move from a count). A\n    direction word bound to a marked change value ('rose 37 points', 'up 4 points', '45% fewer') gives that value's\n    sign, so a wrong sign is a wrong number.\n  FRAMING: you need something beyond the cited cells to see it: the window or period words, the base, the scope\n    (length, platform, weekday, saved or opened, a topic filter), a rank, tie, order, first or last, list\n    completeness, only/all, most/mostly, hidden private rows, or a direction or comparison word with no marked\n    change value ('grew', 'slowed to 142 from 44', 'more than', 'held steady', 'a little').\n  POLICY: outside knowledge, feelings and motives, outcomes, watch time, sensitive topics, limits talk, a weak match,\n    repeating a fact already said.\n  ARGUABLE: the case where the rule can be read both ways; reported both ways, never relabelled after a run."
}
